 \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328264 1113 #uuid "3957a55d-35bf-5e6d-bbac-473c2a705ba0" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328264 1145 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328266 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328267 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328268 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328269 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328270 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1041 "selection" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328266 13194139535038 true] [17592186328265 1110 #uuid "9f7479bf-08b1-5a45-965d-a8bb1206cb98" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328266 1034 "$|B|$ only" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535038 true] [17592186328266 1111 #uuid "09325067-d3bc-5f04-8d3c-42f848520daa" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328267 1034 "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535038 true] [17592186328267 1111 #uuid "73432917-0745-51cc-bb2a-a9748f8c9acb" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328268 1034 "$|C|$ only" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535038 true] [17592186328268 1111 #uuid "e897e5c6-8fe7-5f41-a227-489f0fbebb4e" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328269 1034 "$|A|$ only" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535038 true] [17592186328269 1111 #uuid "cb8f6ba4-d2d7-5c00-a125-3b227b4dcea2" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328270 1034 "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535038 true] [17592186328270 1111 #uuid "a34be7d6-e90d-5883-97a1-acfb9835e535" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328271 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328272 13194139535038 true] [17592186328271 1089 "q-82290" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328271 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535038 true] [17592186328271 1100 "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328271 1113 #uuid "3127bd8b-ed40-56ad-8355-fdaea133207c" 13194139535038 true] [17592186328271 1145 "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139535038 true] [17592186328272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328273 13194139535038 true] [17592186328272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328274 13194139535038 true] [17592186328272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328275 13194139535038 true] [17592186328272 1000 #edb/ref 175921863